{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":17828291,"ns":0,"title":"Barkhausen stability criterion","extract":"In electronics, the Barkhausen stability criterion is a mathematical condition to determine when a linear electronic circuit will oscillate. It was put forth in 1921 by German physicist Heinrich Barkhausen (1881–1956).","description":"Condition determining when a linear electronic circuit will oscillate","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}